{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration and obstacle-recovery policy in specifications. The policy gives one controllable action per decision/recovery state, keeps all uncontrollable events defined at every state, treats obstacle events as safety-critical in commit states, uses backward motion only in a dedicated front-obstacle escape state, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated last-resort stuck state after repeated front blockage.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in G",
    "Use specification automata to bind clear sensing to forward-biased exploration and obstacle sensing to brief directed recovery",
    "Add one-shot commit states so open-loop pulses execute unless preempted by safety-critical obstacle events",
    "Use move_backward only from a dedicated front recovery state and full_rotate only from a dedicated stuck/last_resort state"
  ],
